# MKRT -- build the shared V6 runtime, ON RealXV6, into /src/rt.
#
#     cd /src/rt ; drun mkrt
#
# /src/rt is the one copy of the runtime every other build links against --
# /src/desmet (the toolchain) and /src/usr (the user programs).  They reach
# it as ../rt/NAME in their BIND lists, and -L../rt/ for the library, so
# nothing is duplicated into the image.
#
# Why this works despite C88 having no usable include search here: the
# runtime is compiled IN this directory, so its `#include "UNIX.H"` resolves
# in the cwd with no -i at all.  Only /src/usr and the two converters in
# /src/desmet need -i../rt/, and because every source in the tree spells it
# "UNIX.H" in UPPER case while this directory is lower-case `rt`, the
# prefixed name ../rt/UNIX.H matches VERBATIM -- DCOMPAT's case fold never
# has to run, and it could not help if it did: foldcase() rewrites the whole
# path, so ../rt/unix.h would fold to ../RT/UNIX.H and miss the directory.
#
# Two CRT0s, and each link picks one -- the same split UCOMPAT.C/DCOMPAT.C
# make, for the same reason.  CRT0 returns the kernel's -errno, which is what
# V6 userland reads (usr/unix.h has EAGAIN -11; forktest does `pid ==
# EAGAIN`), so ../usr links it.  DCRT0 returns -1 with the code in ERRNO_,
# which is what the vintage tools' 126 `== -1` tests need, so ../desmet links
# it.  Either way it must be FIRST in the link: BIND -A starts at the first
# instruction of the first object, and d2a patches ENDBRK_ at DS:000A.

asm88 CRT0
asm88 DCRT0
asm88 V6MISC
asm88 SETEXIT
c88 SYSCALL
c88 USTR
c88 PRINTF
c88 DCOMPAT
c88 V6DOS
c88 V6CHAIN
c88 ULIB
c88 UCOMPAT
c88 CTIME
echo === RT BUILT ===
